From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Implement functions popular programs import that aborted them (import sweep, batch 1).

From the unimplemented-import sweep of ~40 freeware programs (outbox/import-sweep.md): each of these
was an 'unimplemented function' import or a '@ stub' that ended the program when called. Now, as
documented: NCryptCreateClaim answers NTE_NOT_SUPPORTED (Chrome, Brave, Signal, Vivaldi);
SetCredentialsAttributesA/W (secur32, sspicli) answer SEC_E_UNSUPPORTED_FUNCTION for valid
credentials (msquic); ResolveIpNetEntry2 answers from the neighbor table (msquic);
I_RpcOpenClientProcess opens the local client's process with the server's own token (Chrome's and
Brave's elevation services); MFCreateTranscodeTopology says E_NOTIMPL with no topology (Zoom);
WlanGetNetworkBssList lists the networks the scan sees, BSSIDs unknown (Zoom); the Fwpm
filter/provider/transaction/sublayer calls fail as FwpmEngineOpen0 does, adding nothing (Brave's
VPN service); InternetSetCookieEx2 sets the cookie its parts make (PotPlayer). Header declarations
added for the new ones.
---
